{"tool_name":"speedygenesxl","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"speedygenesxl","home":"https://github.com/neilswainston/SpeedyGenesXL","license":"Not licensed","summary":"An Automated, High-Throughput Platform for the Preparation of Bespoke Ultralarge Variant Libraries for Directed Evolution.","addition_date":"2022-09-01T12:26:39.322597Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T15:44:41.444776Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:speedygenesxl","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"dbk@liv.ac.uk","name":"Douglas B. Kell","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Andrew Currin"},{"name":"Joanna C. Sadler"},{"name":"Mark S. Dunstan"},{"name":"Neil Swainston"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Primer removal","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3237"},{"term":"Sequence assembly","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0310"}]}],"name":"SpeedyGenesXL","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1007/978-1-0716-2152-3_5","metadata":{"abstract":"Directed evolution of proteins is a highly effective strategy for tailoring biocatalysts to a particular application, and is capable of engineering improvements such as kcat, thermostability and organic solvent tolerance. It is recognized that large and systematic libraries are required to navigate a protein\u2019s vast and rugged sequence landscape effectively, yet their preparation is nontrivial and commercial libraries are extremely costly. To address this, we have developed SpeedyGenesXL, an automated, high-throughput platform for the production of wild-type genes, Boolean OR, combinatorial, or combinatorial-OR-type libraries based on the SpeedyGenes methodology. Together this offers a flexible platform for library synthesis, capable of generating many different bespoke, diverse libraries simultaneously.","authors":[{"name":"Currin A."},{"name":"Duns